  "memo": "The Boeing Company closed its most recent fiscal year on a high note, demonstrating resilience as commercial aviation demand fully recovered and defense spending accelerated. In fiscal 2024, total revenue reached $77.1 billion, up roughly three percent year-over-year, while net income climbed to $5.9 billion, reflecting an expanding operating margin near eight percent. Diluted earnings per share came in at $5.88, marking a significant rebound from the severe pandemic troughs seen in prior years. Operating cash flow remained robust at $10.5 billion, supporting continued debt reduction and potential capital return programs. Comparing these results to fiscal 2023, when revenue was $74.1 billion and net income was $5.3 billion, highlights the steady operational improvement over the last two years. Boeing’s strategic shift toward sustainable aviation fuel and increased defense contracts provides a durable tailwind. We view BA as a classic value recovery story with a constructive long-term trajectory as production rates normalize and free cash flow scales."
